From: Codex <codex@local>
Subject: [PATCH] net: dsa: qca8k: add QCA8386 ID-only diagnostic stop

This is a RAM-test-only diagnostic patch.  Log the validated QCA8386 ID
and revision, then stop before dsa_register_switch() can change port,
header, VLAN, or forwarding state.  It distinguishes a harmful MHT ID
access from a later DSA setup failure.  Do not carry this patch into a
production image.

---
 drivers/net/dsa/qca/qca8k-8xxx.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/net/dsa/qca/qca8k-8xxx.c b/drivers/net/dsa/qca/qca8k-8xxx.c
--- a/drivers/net/dsa/qca/qca8k-8xxx.c
+++ b/drivers/net/dsa/qca/qca8k-8xxx.c
@@ -2287,6 +2287,14 @@ static int qca8k_sw_probe(struct mdio_device *mdiodev)
 	ret = qca8k_read_switch_id(priv);
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
+
+	if (priv->switch_id == QCA8K_ID_QCA8386) {
+		dev_info(priv->dev,
+			 "ID-only diagnostic validated id %x revision %x; stopping before DSA registration\n",
+			 priv->switch_id, priv->switch_revision);
+		return -ENODEV;
+	}
+
 
 	priv->ds = devm_kzalloc(&mdiodev->dev, sizeof(*priv->ds), GFP_KERNEL);
 	if (!priv->ds)
-- 
